    {"step": 1, "tactic": "Resource Development / Acquire Infrastructure — Domains", "technique": "T1583.001", "what_happened": "At 2026-05-12 09:14:07 CEST, Sysmon on internal host WIN-FINANCE-83 (10.108.57.83) logged Event ID 22 (DnsQuery) for data.win.eventdata.queryName=corp-portaI.com — a homoglyph typosquat of the legitimate corp-portal.com (capital 'I' substituted for lowercase 'l'). Wazuh rule fired with rule.mitre.id=T1583.001 (Acquire Infrastructure: Domains). The query is the first of a sequential burst of 8 lookalike-domain resolutions from the same host against the corporate DNS resolver 10.108.57.1, each ~4 seconds apart. The fact that an internal endpoint is actively resolving an adversary-registered lookalike domain is the detection surface for the attacker's domain-acquisition (T1583.001) staging — the domains exist and are now DNS-resolvable, and a corporate host is reaching them.", "chain_reason": "Sysmon Event ID 22 with data.win.eventdata.queryName matching a known homoglyph/combosquat pattern of the corporate brand. Wazuh enrichment rule attached rule.mitre.id=T1583.001 because the queried domain is on the newly-registered-lookalike watchlist.", "first_seen": "2026-05-12T09:14:07+0200"},
